From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:39:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Style with Tailwind

Dress the pages in Tailwind CSS. No Node, no npm: maago tailwind runs
Tailwind CSS's standalone binary (a pinned version, fetched once into
the user cache, its checksum checked).

- board/tailwind.css: the input. source(none) and @source "./templates"
  look for classes in the board's templates alone; the copied auth's
  pages stay as they are
- board/static/tailwind.css: the output of maago tailwind. Nobody
  writes it, but it is committed (a plain file, not marked generated).
  maago check does not see whether it is stale, so after changing the
  classes in a template, run maago tailwind again

base.html links it with {{static "board/tailwind.css"}}. Each app's
static/ files are served at /static/<app>/, and the link names the file
with a hash of its content. Browsers do not ask for that name again for
a year; new content gets a new name, so no stale CSS stays. Under the
prefix /app it is /app/static/board/tailwind.<hash>.css.

